course: dictionary
lesson: 7193
title: Pests: animals and annoying people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives two meanings for pest, and the words around it tell you which one is meant. Ask yourself: is this about crops, food and homes, or about a person who keeps bothering you?
explain: «People call pest experts or set traps away from children and pets.» Here a pest is an animal that harms things, such as mice or cockroaches. Pests can eat our food, damage homes and spread germs.
explain: Now read: «Stop being a pest and let me finish my book!» This pest is a person, usually a child, who keeps annoying you. Try swapping in your meaning. Does the sentence still make sense?
fact: A pest is an insect or animal that harms crops, food, gardens or homes.
fact: Rats, mice, cockroaches and greenfly are all pests.
fact: A pest can also be an annoying person, especially a child who keeps bothering you.
fact: «Pest control» means stopping pests from causing harm, using traps, sprays or natural enemies such as ladybirds.
fact: In Chinese, «xiǎo pìhái» means brat or little pest. Adults use it about naughty children, and it is a bit rude.
exercise: «Pests eat our food, damage homes or carry germs.» What is a pest in this sentence? | A person who keeps bothering you | *An insect or animal that harms food and homes | A very large house | A kind of food that children like
exercise: «Stop being a pest and let me finish my book!» What does pest mean here? | A garden tool | A rat in the kitchen | *An annoying person, especially a child who keeps bothering you | An insect that eats crops
exercise: Which of these is a pest in a garden? | Frog | Ladybird | *Greenfly | Sunflower
test: «Pest experts put traps along walls because mice travel there.» In this sentence, which thing is the pest? | Traps | Experts | *Mice | Walls
test: Why might someone say «Don't be such a pest»? | Because the person is a pest expert | *Because the person keeps bothering them | Because the person is helping in the garden | Because the person is a spider
exam: Which meaning fits «Spiders in homes eat flies, mosquitoes and other pests»? | *An insect or animal that harms crops, food, gardens or homes | A kind of spider web | An annoying person | A trap for mice
